From: Rob Watson <rob@mediaeden.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gs-app-query: make the dedupe-flags property a guint64

GsAppListFilterFlags is deliberately a 64-bit enum (its MASK member is
G_MAXUINT64 and gs-app-list.h static-asserts sizeof == sizeof (guint64)),
so every gs_app_query_new() caller pushes a 64-bit value for
"dedupe-flags". The property itself, however, is registered with
g_param_spec_flags(), whose GValue collector reads a 32-bit int.

On 64-bit ABIs that mismatch goes unnoticed. On 32-bit ARM the 64-bit
argument is 8-byte aligned, so g_object_new_valist() reads the padding
slot as the value and the real value as the next property name, and
gnome-software segfaults in g_param_spec_pool_lookup() as soon as the
overview page is loaded (observed on postmarketOS armv7 with 50.3;
same symptom as https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-software/-/issues/1007).

Register the property as a guint64, matching the header's contract.

--- a/lib/gs-app-query.c
+++ b/lib/gs-app-query.c
@@ -251,7 +251,7 @@
 		g_value_set_uint (value, self->max_results);
 		break;
 	case PROP_DEDUPE_FLAGS:
-		g_value_set_flags (value, self->dedupe_flags);
+		g_value_set_uint64 (value, self->dedupe_flags);
 		break;
 	case PROP_SORT_FUNC:
 		g_value_set_pointer (value, self->sort_func);
@@ -358,7 +358,7 @@
 	case PROP_DEDUPE_FLAGS:
 		/* Construct only. */
 		g_assert (self->dedupe_flags == 0);
-		self->dedupe_flags = g_value_get_flags (value);
+		self->dedupe_flags = g_value_get_uint64 (value);
 		break;
 	case PROP_SORT_FUNC:
 		/* Construct only. */
@@ -604,11 +604,11 @@
 	 * Since: 43
 	 */
 	props[PROP_DEDUPE_FLAGS] =
-		g_param_spec_flags ("dedupe-flags", "Dedupe Flags",
-				    "Flags to specify how to deduplicate the returned apps, if at all.",
-				    GS_TYPE_APP_LIST_FILTER_FLAGS, GS_APP_LIST_FILTER_FLAG_NONE,
-				    G_PARAM_READWRITE | G_PARAM_CONSTRUCT_ONLY |
-				    G_PARAM_STATIC_STRINGS | G_PARAM_EXPLICIT_NOTIFY);
+		g_param_spec_uint64 ("dedupe-flags", "Dedupe Flags",
+				     "Flags to specify how to deduplicate the returned apps, if at all.",
+				     0, G_MAXUINT64, GS_APP_LIST_FILTER_FLAG_NONE,
+				     G_PARAM_READWRITE | G_PARAM_CONSTRUCT_ONLY |
+				     G_PARAM_STATIC_STRINGS | G_PARAM_EXPLICIT_NOTIFY);
 
 	/**
 	 * GsAppQuery:sort-func: (nullable)
